## Out of scope for phase9 (intentionally deferred)

- **Per-user retrieval isolation** — `services/retrieval.py::retrieve_top_k` should filter the pgvector ANN query by `user_id` so the tutor only grounds answers in the caller's documents. Today's CAP/Raft/CRDT cross-pollination across users is the same surface that exists pre-Phase-9; Phase 9 just made it possible to see it. **This is the most important next step** for multi-tenant correctness.
- **Pagination + search on the documents table** — current implementation is `ORDER BY created_at DESC` over the whole user's corpus. Fine for personal use; will need a `limit/offset` + a name filter once the table exceeds ~100 rows. Skeleton already supports it (the route uses SQLAlchemy `select(...)` — just add `.limit().offset()`).
- **Per-document edit (rename, retag)** — not requested for Phase 9. The schema supports it (`Document.title`, `Document.doc_metadata` are mutable), but no UI affordance exists. Would be a `PATCH /documents/{id}` route + an edit modal.
- **Bulk delete** — the UI only supports one-row-at-a-time. A checkbox column + "Delete selected" would be trivial on top of the current table but adds a confirmation-UX question (single toast vs per-row) that wasn't part of the Phase 9 ask.
- **Backfilling legacy `NULL` rows automatically** — no migration heuristic could pick the right owner (the pre-Phase-9 ingests were genuinely shared). Left to the operator via SQL.
- **Document soft-delete + restore** — currently `DELETE /documents/{id}` is a hard delete (chunks cascade). A soft-delete column + a 30-day grace window would prevent accidents at the cost of breaking the CASCADE simplicity. Deferred until a user actually wants it.
- **Audit trail of deletions** — no `documents_deleted` log table; once gone, gone. Add when compliance asks.
- **Rate limiting `DELETE /documents/{id}`** — a malicious authenticated client could enumerate UUIDs hoping to find one to delete. Currently mitigated by the 404-not-403 collapse (no oracle), but a per-user rate limit would still be defence-in-depth. Belongs with the broader rate-limiting work in ARCHITECTURE §8.

